    "updated_at": "2020-02-03T19:01:08Z",
    "body": "I think Startship cannot do this right now (hopefully someone will correct me if I'm wrong) but it's indeed a very useful thing to have. In Powerlevel10k the API for this feature looks like this: https://github.com/romkatv/powerlevel10k/blob/637752ef7bc790c4d8f6ff0498d1e70496ff9a96/config/p10k-lean.zsh#L819-L844. It's been working pretty well. Basically, you define a pattern that allows you to assign *classes* to different kubernetes contexts and then you define colors and icons for different classes.\r\n\r\nHope this helps!",
